        "title": "[codex] fix(sessions): report archive cleanup in sessions cleanup",
        "body": "Fixes #75658\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`openclaw sessions cleanup --dry-run` did not preview stale `.deleted.*` and `.reset.*` archive files, and the apply summary did not report when those physical archive files were removed. Operators could see only unreferenced-artifact counts even when deleted/reset session archives were consuming disk.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Reuse the configured archive-retention rules for cleanup preview and apply reporting.\n- Run archive preview before disk-budget simulation and exclude already-attributed archive paths from later cleanup phases.\n- Preserve configured archive retention when cleanup runs through the SQLite lifecycle boundary.\n- Resolve archive directories correctly for direct per-agent SQLite targets.\n- Deduplicate shared-directory archive previews and keep per-agent applied summaries aligned with their targets.\n- Clear reset-archive discovery caches and notify transcript subscribers after successful archive deletion, including the source transcript path needed by connected history streams.\n- Count only successful deletions; dry-run never emits mutation notifications.\n- Extract archive coordination and reset-archive cache bookkeeping so changed legacy TypeScript files satisfy the repository LOC ratchet.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers running `sessions cleanup` now see deleted/reset archive cleanup in dry-run and apply output. Forced cleanup scans the canonical archive directory even when no session rows were removed, while `resetArchiveRetention: false` still preserves reset archives.\n\n## Exact-Head Evidence\n\nRebased onto `main` at `301a4bf6273`; pushed head `cf171c43450`.\n\n- Focused cleanup/accessor/archive suite: 8 files, 143 tests passed.\n- `pnpm check:loc --base origin/main --head HEAD` passed for all 12 changed production TypeScript files.\n- Repository `oxfmt` and type-aware `run-oxlint.mjs` wrappers passed on all touched TypeScript files.\n- Session accessor boundary guard passed without increasing the debt baseline.\n- Dead-code unused-file and unused-export guards passed.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Exact-head Codex review against `origin/main` completed with no actionable findings.\n\nReal CLI proof on this exact head, with the temporary path redacted:\n\n```text\n$ openclaw sessions cleanup --store \"$TMP/archive-store/sessions.json\" --dry-run --enforce\nSession store: $TMP/archive-store/sessions.json\nMaintenance mode: enforce\nEntries: 0 -> 0 (remove 0)\nWould prune missing transcripts: 0\nWould retire stale direct DM sessions: 0\nWould prune stale model-run probes: 0\nWould prune stale: 0\nWould cap overflow: 0\nWould prune deleted/reset archives: 2\nWould prune unreferenced artifacts: 0\n\nafter dry-run:\nfresh.jsonl.deleted.2026-07-12T00-00-00.000Z\nold.jsonl.deleted.2026-01-01T00-00-00.000Z\nold.jsonl.reset.2026-01-01T00-00-00.000Z\nsessions.json\n\n$ openclaw sessions cleanup --store \"$TMP/archive-store/sessions.json\" --enforce\nSession store: $TMP/archive-store/sessions.json\nApplied maintenance. Current entries: 0\nPruned deleted/reset archives: 2\n\nafter apply:\nfresh.jsonl.deleted.2026-07-12T00-00-00.000Z\nopenclaw-agent.sqlite\nsessions.json\n```\n\n## AI Assistance\n\nAI-assisted: yes. Codex was used to inspect the issue and contributor rules, implement the patch, resolve review findings and current-main rebases, run focused validation and real CLI proof, and review the exact head.\n",
